// ╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║  15 — Variable Lifetimes & Negative Lifetime Hoisting        ║
// ╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
//
// Variables can be given a lifetime <N> — they expire after N
// statements. When N is negative, the variable is "hoisted"
// backward: it becomes available N lines BEFORE its declaration.

// ── Negative lifetime hoisting ──────────────────────────────────
// The variable `name` is used BEFORE it's declared,
// because its <-1> lifetime hoists it one line upward:
print name!
const const name<-1> = "Luke"!

// ── Positive lifetime ───────────────────────────────────────────
// This variable lasts exactly 3 statements:
var x <3> = 10!
print x!
print x!
print x!
